     "texto": "putting into questions the well accepted capital asset pricing model (CAPM)",
     "doc_id": 18
    },
    {
     "texto": "the multifractal nature of ﬁnancial markets contradict the EMH, and thus the Black-Scholes pricing model and its associated assumptions",
     "doc_id": 19
    },
    {
     "texto": "The academic basis of market prediction studies is still the Efficient Market Hypothesis (EMH) that asserts that assets promptly reflect the information accessible and thus constrain the prospect of systematically outperforming the market",
     "doc_id": 32
    },
    {
     "texto": "HFT's arbitrage activities ensure market balance by quickly correcting abnormal price differences in the market. This supports the efficient pricing mechanism envisaged by EMH.",
     "doc_id": 171
    },
    {
     "texto": "Classical finance theory such as the Efficient Market Hypothesis suggests it is impossible to consistently beat the market without taking additional risk(s).",
     "doc_id": 385
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
