  {
   "id": "gradient boosting",
   "nombre_canonico": "gradient boosting",
   "tipo": "metodo",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "gradient boosting"
   ],
   "menciones": 4,
   "doc_frecuencia": 4,
   "doc_ids": [
    1,
    99,
    214,
    345
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "LightGBM se usa como estimador de regresión dentro del framework AutoML para evaluar y rankear las features generadas por el LLM.",
     "doc_id": 1
    },
    {
     "texto": "XGBoost usado como baseline de comparación; el paper reporta 92.40% accuracy para XGBoost vs 97.21% del DWH-RRFC propuesto.",
     "doc_id": 99
    },
    {
     "texto": "Técnica de ensemble learning basada en árboles de decisión que construye modelos secuencialmente corrigiendo errores residuales. El paper cita a Krauss et al. (2017) para justificar que los frameworks basados en árboles producen resultados superiores a redes neuronales en statistical arbitrage.",
     "doc_id": 214
    },
    {
     "texto": "Gradient Boosting classifier con identical features y training data que Random Forest. Muestra near-identical error trajectories (correlación 0.94-0.99), confirmando la hipótesis de correlated failure.",
     "doc_id": 345
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "FLAML is used to train a regression model (with LightGBM as the estimator) on the extracted feature matrix.",
     "doc_id": 1
    },
    {
     "texto": "XG Boost: Accuracy 92.40%, Precision 89.17%, Recall 94.90%, F1 Score 91.95%",
     "doc_id": 99
    },
    {
     "texto": "Krauss et al. (2017) concludes that frameworks that rely on trees produce superior results compared to ANNs such as RNNs, while being faster to train.",
     "doc_id": 214
    },
    {
     "texto": "both models exhibit near-identical error trajectories throughout the test period: the inter-model error correlation is 0.99 during stable pre-crash conditions and 0.94 during the crash.",
     "doc_id": 345
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
