     "tipo_original": "CAUSA",
     "objeto_texto": "downward bias in β",
     "doc_id": 226,
     "revisar": false
    },
    {
     "tipo": "MITIGA",
     "tipo_original": "MITIGA",
     "objeto_texto": "including limit order flows in regressions",
     "doc_id": 226,
     "revisar": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "information acquisition",
   "nombre_canonico": "information acquisition",
   "tipo": "fenomeno",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "Information Acquisition",
    "information acquisition"
   ],
   "menciones": 2,
   "doc_frecuencia": 2,
   "doc_ids": [
    41,
    186
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Actividad de adquisición de información por parte de participantes del mercado, proxied por descargas no-robot de datos de reporte financiero desde EDGAR de la SEC; AT puede fomentarla o desalentarla según el tipo de estrategia.",
     "doc_id": 41
    },
    {
     "texto": "Decisión ex-ante de los traders de invertir en información privada. Trading delays más largos debilitan estos incentivos, reduciendo la fracción de equilibrio de informed traders.",
     "doc_id": 186
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "we find a positive association between AT and the number of non-robot downloads of financial data from the SEC EDGAR database, suggesting that AT encourages overall information acquisition in the market",
     "doc_id": 41
    },
    {
     "texto": "Traders' information acquisition incentives are weaker if trading delays are longer. Therefore, the equilibrium fraction of informed traders is lower if trading delays are longer.",
     "doc_id": 186
    }
   ],
   "relaciones_crudas": [
    {
     "tipo": "MIDE",
     "tipo_original": "MIDE",
     "objeto_texto": "revelatory price efficiency",
     "doc_id": 41,
